{
  "fixture_version": 2,
  "purpose": "Neutral cross-language vectors for the transaction nonce bound of RFC 0006 section 6 step 2, and for the Transfer and Stake encodings. Pins the signing bytes, signatures, full encodings and hashes at the nonce and amount boundaries, malformed encodings that must not decode, signatures over the wrong message, and state-transition outcomes at the bound. Version 2 (RFC 0006 section 2, S1-5): every signature is over \"mbongo-tx:v2\" || chain_id || the transaction fields, for the dev chain below; the fields and the state transitions are those of version 1.",
  "supersedes": "test-vectors/transaction/nonce-boundary-v1.json",
  "chain": {
    "chain_id": "2fd700acc09b3d1752ca6fe21e7d6f4844917c5a9fcd41a34fe1d13d7deed1a4",
    "chain_id_source": "crates/mbongo-core/genesis/dev.json, the dev genesis: chain_id = BLAKE3(\"mbongo:chain-id:v1\" || file_bytes)",
    "signing_domain": {
      "ascii": "mbongo-tx:v2",
      "hex": "6d626f6e676f2d74783a7632",
      "length": 12
    },
    "other_chain_id": "5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a",
    "other_chain_id_use": "no signature in this file verifies for it: a signature for one network does not verify on another"
  },
  "authority": {
    "state_transition": "docs/rfcs/0006-chain-identity-authenticated-blocks.md, section 6, step 2",
    "nonce_bound": "Step 2 adds one to the sender's nonce. A nonce of u64::MAX has no successor, so a transaction whose nonce equals u64::MAX is refused with InvalidNonce (implementation note C-3 on PR #211, which does not change the accepted design). The largest applicable nonce is therefore u64::MAX - 1.",
    "transaction_structure": "crates/mbongo-core/src/primitives.rs: Transaction, TransactionType, TransactionPayload, Transaction::signed_fields, Transaction::signing_payload(chain_id)",
    "signing_domain": "docs/rfcs/0006-chain-identity-authenticated-blocks.md, section 2",
    "transaction_hash": "crates/mbongo-node/src/backend.rs: compute_tx_hash, BLAKE3 over the full SCALE encoding",
    "receipt": "test-vectors/receipt/receipt-v1.json, referenced and never duplicated"
  },
  "conventions": {
    "hex": "lowercase, no 0x prefix",
    "integers": "amount and nonce are decimal strings, because values above 2^53 do not survive a JSON number",
    "byte_order": "fixed-width integers are little-endian and never compact",
    "test_key": "<test_key> means the key of test-vectors/receipt/receipt-v1.json test_key: seed 0x2a repeated 32 times, TEST ONLY",
    "receipt_reference": "receipt_vector names a vector in test-vectors/receipt/receipt-v1.json; <receipt.executor> resolves there"
  },
  "derivation": {
    "method": "Every expected value was built from the protocol rules, not by encoding with production Rust or the SDK. Byte layouts by hand as concatenated fields; integers by explicit little-endian construction; signatures by Ed25519 from OpenSSL (node:crypto); hashes by a BLAKE3 written from the specification. Both primitives were first checked against published values (BLAKE3 reference vectors, RFC 8032 test 1) and against every vector of test-vectors/transaction/anchor-receipt-v1.json.",
    "upstream_truth": "test-vectors/receipt/receipt-v1.json and crates/mbongo-core/genesis/dev.json (for chain_id) are the only machine inputs.",
    "version_2": "The S1-1 derivation of version 1, with each signature made over \"mbongo-tx:v2\" || chain_id || fields instead of the bare fields, and checked to verify for chain_id only: not over the bare fields, not for other_chain_id."
  },
